How to create multiple envronments using terraform
=======================================

When working with Infrastructure as Code (IaC), one of the key challenges is managing multiple environments — like dev, staging, and prod — efficiently and safely.

Here are 3 common approaches to do this using Terraform.
1.Using .tfvars Files
Create separate variable files like dev.tfvars, staging.tfvars, and prod.tfvars.
Run Terraform with:
terraform apply -var-file="dev.tfvars"
Simple and easy for small-scale setups
Can get messy when scaling to many environments

2.Using Workspaces
Terraform Workspaces allow you to manage multiple states from the same configuration.
Commands:
terraform workspace new dev
terraform workspace select prod
Centralized codebase

Limited flexibility for very different configurations

3.Using Separate Repos + Modules
Keep a core module repo for reusable infra code
Create separate environment repos (dev-infra, prod-infra) that call those modules
Best for large teams & production-grade systems
